<title>UK: Chelsea Village up after FA Cup victory.</title>
<headline>Chelsea Village up after FA Cup victory.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Chelsea Village Plc, owner of the English premiership football club, rose on Monday after Chelsea secured a place in the FA Cup final with Sunday's 3-0 victory over Wimbledon.</p>
<p>The stock was up 10p at 128-1/2 by 0748 GMT.</p>
<p>Chelsea's victory clears the way for the club to take part in lucrative European competition next season.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
